ide I'm just gonna let  it simmer and all come together while I  heat up and toast some pepitas so just a  little bit of olive oil in the pan  and we've got some beautiful pumpkin  seeds or pepitas as they're often called  and I'm also gonna add in some fresh  sage this is one of my favorite favorite  herbs  [Music]  and finally my mushroom broccoli soup so  this starts with this jiggly concoction  cream of mushroom soup the soup that  nobody really understands why it exists  but here it is alas finding its way into  recipes and housewives homes everywhere  I promise I will make this edible so  next we're gonna add in some evaporated  milk and I like this because it's really  so much creamier but at the same time  really really light and low-fat okay so  next I'm gonna add in some fresh chopped  broccoli and I like to chop it nice and  fine so that way it cooks really really  quickly in the soup okay now I'm gonna  add in a can of white beans some cooked  quinoa and I'm just gonna stir this all  together until it turns into a nice  creamy thick luxurious student okay so  while this is bubbling away and the  broccoli is just softening up and  getting tender I'm going to pop a couple  little whole-grain crostinis under the  broiler with a little bit of sharp  cheddar on top  thank you guys so much for watching I  hope you enjoyed these fun little canned  soup hacks if you did be sure to give  this video the thumbs up leave me a  comment below with some of your favorite  pantry staples  I totally will breathe some new life  into them and give them a little  makeover also don't forget to subscribe  to the channel and I'll see you next  time on Abby's kitchen  [Music]
 

